    LLM: 'Standard trick-taking: 1. Must follow suit if possible. 2. If void in led suit, may play any card. 3. Highest card of the led suit wins the trick. 4. There are no trumps. 5. Winner leads to the next trick.',
    Player: 'Standard trick-taking: 1. Must follow suit if possible. 2. If void in led suit, may play any card. 3. Highest card of the led suit wins the trick. 4. There are no trumps. 5. Winner leads to the next trick.',
    objective: 'Score the fewest points. Avoid capturing the Queen of Spades (50 points) and minimize capture of other point cards.',
    gameplay: 'Standard trick-taking: 1. Must follow suit if possible. 2. If void in led suit, may play any card. 3. Highest card of the led suit wins the trick. 4. There are no trumps. 5. Winner leads to the next trick.',
    keyRules: [
      'Queen of Spades = 50 points penalty.',
      'Ace = 11 points, Ten = 10 points, King = 4 points, Queen = 3 points, Jack = 2 points.',
      '7, 8, 9 = 0 points.',
      'Must follow suit if possible.',
      "The Queen of Spades can be played at any time once a player is void in the led suit, even if they hold other spades (the 'Laus' rule).",
      'Game ends when a player reaches 100 or 150 points (agreed beforehand). Lowest score wins.',
